```gitignore
# .NET / Visual Studio
bin/
obj/
.vs/
.vscode/

# User-specific files
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Build output
Debug/
Release/
x64/
x86/

# NuGet
packages/
*.nupkg
*.snupkg

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pfx

# Local AI data
memory/
conversations/
experiences/
core/permissions/permissions.json

# Local model/cache files
models/
ollama/
*.gguf

# Temporary files
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp

# IDE
.idea/

# Test results
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage/
```

I would **not** commit your agent's personal memory, conversations, or experiences to Git, since those may eventually contain private information.
